  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DEC Phase 2 - Enhancing the ability of older people including those with disabilities to recover from the 2022 floods in Pakistan.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To contribute towards the recovery and rehabilitation of the livelihoods of flood affected House Holds including older people and people with disabilities and increase their resilience to climate change impactsThis will be achieved through the following four outcomes:Outcome A - Vulnerable floods affected households comprising older people, people with disabilities and their families have increased access to livelihood activities and experience sustained improvements in their livelihoods.Outcome B &#x2013; At risk older women and men have improved access to mental health and psychosocial support and assistive technology that strengthens independent living and their engagement in livelihood activities.Outcome C - Capacities of selected disaster-prone communities are strengthened to develop community adaptation plans and increase their resilience for future disasters.Outcome D - Government and humanitarian agencies recognise and respond to the needs of older women and men in emergencies and disaster preparedness.</narrative>
  </description>
